  "material_learning": "Low realized-skewness admission was not an independent economic improvement for DRA V1. Although the frozen nonredundancy gate narrowly passed against realized performance in Design, the primary vetoed 171 Design and 92 Validation signals, lost 43.56 USDT of Design total PnL and 31.79 USDT of Validation total PnL, worsened Validation drawdown by 2.57 percentage points, lengthened median and P90 holding, and lost total PnL in every annual fold. Both stricter and looser neighbors also lost Validation realized and total PnL and failed path-risk gates.",
  "scientific_claim": "For the exact complete-day H1 realized-skewness estimator, prior-twenty-day midrank normalization, low-skew relation, 0.5 primary and 0.3/0.7 neighbors applied only to unchanged equal-capital DRA V1 entries, historical Design and Validation evidence through 2024 rejects candidate status.",
